does (?i) match?          perl 5, anchored
pattern   subject                                        /i   /ia   /iaa
k         U+004B LATIN CAPITAL LETTER K                  yes  yes   yes
k         U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes  yes   no
s         U+017F LATIN SMALL LETTER LONG S               yes  yes   no
U+00DF    U+1E9E LATIN CAPITAL LETTER SHARP S            yes  yes   yes
U+1E9E    U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S              yes  yes   yes
ss        U+00DF LATIN SMALL LETTER SHARP S              yes  yes   no
[k]       U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes  yes   no
[a-z]     U+212A KELVIN SIGN                             yes  yes   no
i         U+0131 LATIN SMALL LETTER DOTLESS I            no   no    no
i         U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   no   no    no
i U+0307  U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE   yes  yes   no

does (?i) fold the BACKREFERENCE comparison too?
(?i)(a)\1    vs 'a' + U+0041            yes
(?i)(k)\1    vs 'k' + U+212A            yes

one program, two answers about the same pair
  fc: U+00DF eq 'ss'                    true    regex /i: yes
  fc: U+212A eq 'k'                     true    regex /i: yes
  fc: U+017F eq 's'                     true    regex /i: yes
  lc(U+1E9E) eq U+00DF                  true    regex /i: yes
  uc(U+00DF) is 2 code points           true    regex /i: yes
